eaching Plan.\\n\\nChoose a compact ordered sequence of the six primitives only:\\n  paragraph | heading | list | figure | table | callout\\n\\nReturn CHOICES only \u2014 never full content payloads.\\n\\nHard rules:\\n- No component_id, template_id, page_break, ruled_lines, media blobs, or interaction nodes.\\n- Interactions are authored separately; never invent them here.\\n- One teaching block MAY become MULTIPLE ordinary nodes when pedagogy needs it\\n  (e.g. paragraph + figure + callout for one explain block).\\n- Prefer clear pedagogical order: orient \u2192 explain \u2192 illustrate \u2192 practice cue.\\n- Figure: emit a figure choice with role/reason only. Asset generation uses the\\n  existing figure pipeline \u2014 do not invent image bytes or URLs.\\n- Keep ids stable and unique across the sequence.\\n- Stay within the Teaching Plan objective and must_not_introduce constraints.\\n- Do not decorate every section with tables or callouts \u2014 use them intentionally.\\n- Preserve section_id from the teaching plan so local regeneration stays addressable.\\n\\nReturn JSON exactly:\\n{\\n  \"nodes\": [\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"string\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"string\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"string|null\",\\n      \"kind\": \"paragraph|heading|list|figure|table|callout\",\\n      \"role\": \"string|null\",\\n      \"reason\": \"string\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\n\\n## AUTHORING DEFINITION\\n{\\n  \"assessment\": {},\\n  \"capability_id\": \"document-composer\",\\n  \"converter_ref\": null,\\n  \"definition_hash\": \"1e22585b1bfd0a9c161a2240368dc662784b1b5e4e36dee9d5cc61a32b097b8c\",\\n  \"instructions\": \"You compose ordinary lesson document STRUCTURE from an approved Teaching Plan.\\\\n\\\\nChoose a compact ordered sequence of the six primitives only:\\\\n  paragraph | heading | list | figure | table | callout\\\\n\\\\nReturn CHOICES only \\\\u2014 never full content payloads.\\\\n\\\\nHard rules:\\\\n- No component_id, template_id, page_break, ruled_lines, media blobs, or interaction nodes.\\\\n- Interactions are authored separately; never invent them here.\\\\n- One teaching block MAY become MULTIPLE ordinary nodes when pedagogy needs it\\\\n  (e.g. paragraph + figure + callout for one explain block).\\\\n- Prefer clear pedagogical order: orient \\\\u2192 explain \\\\u2192 illustrate \\\\u2192 practice cue.\\\\n- Figure: emit a figure choice with role/reason only. Asset generation uses the\\\\n  existing figure pipeline \\\\u2014 do not invent image bytes or URLs.\\\\n- Keep ids stable and unique across the sequence.\\\\n- Stay within the Teaching Plan objective and must_not_introduce constraints.\\\\n- Do not decorate every section with tables or callouts \\\\u2014 use them intentionally.\\\\n- Preserve section_id from the teaching plan so local regeneration stays addressable.\\\\n\\\\nReturn JSON exactly:\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\"nodes\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\"id\\\\\": \\\\\"string\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\"teaching_block_id\\\\\": \\\\\"string\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\"section_id\\\\\": \\\\\"string|null\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\"kind\\\\\": \\\\\"paragraph|heading|list|figure|table|callout\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\"role\\\\\": \\\\\"string|null\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\"reason\\\\\": \\\\\"string\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\\n\",\\n  \"knowledge\": {},\\n  \"modes\": [\\n    \"generate\"\\n  ],\\n  \"native_path\": \"learn\",\\n  \"payload_schema\": {\\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n    \"properties\": {\\n      \"nodes\": {\\n        \"items\": {\\n          \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n          \"properties\": {\\n            \"id\": {\\n              \"minLength\": 1,\\n              \"type\": \"string\"\\n            },\\n            \"kind\": {\\n              \"enum\": [\\n                \"callout\",\\n                \"figure\",\\n                \"heading\",\\n                \"list\",\\n                \"paragraph\",\\n                \"table\"\\n              ],\\n              \"type\": \"string\"\\n            },\\n            \"reason\": {\\n              \"minLength\": 1,\\n              \"type\": \"string\"\\n            },\\n            \"role\": {\\n              \"type\": \"string\"\\n            },\\n            \"section_id\": {\\n              \"type\": \"string\"\\n            },\\n            \"teaching_block_id\": {\\n              \"minLength\": 1,\\n              \"type\": \"string\"\\n            }\\n          },\\n          \"required\": [\\n            \"id\",\\n            \"teaching_block_id\",\\n            \"kind\",\\n            \"reason\"\\n          ],\\n          \"type\": \"object\"\\n        },\\n        \"minItems\": 1,\\n        \"type\": \"array\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \"required\": [\\n      \"nodes\"\\n    ],\\n    \"type\": \"object\"\\n  },\\n  \"required_inputs\": [\\n    \"teaching_plan\"\\n  ],\\n  \"validator_refs\": [\\n    \"document.composer_schema\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\n## SCOPED REQUEST\\n{\\n  \"inputs\": {\\n    \"teaching_plan\": {\\n      \"arc\": \"The lesson opens on the classroom plant on the windowsill beside the cup of water and asks learners to commit to a guess about where its food comes from, so a personal wrong model is on the table. The explanation then fixes the category term \\\\u2014 the plant is a producer, a living thing that makes its own food \\\\u2014 and separates what the plant takes in through its roots from what it makes. The contrast section puts the producer idea against the soil-as-food and water-as-food readings on the same plant so the boundary is visible, and the close checks whether the learner now recognizes the plant, not the soil or the water, as the maker of the food.\",\\n      \"revision\": 1,\\n      \"sections\": [\\n        {\\n          \"blocks\": [\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Present the concrete case: a potted classroom plant on the windowsill, sitting next to a cup of water. Ask learners where they think the plant\\'s food comes from and have them commit to one answer before anything is explained. Do not name soil, water, or sunlight as food, and do not state the target idea that the plant makes its own food.\",\\n              \"evidence\": \"The objective\\'s recognition claim only becomes meaningful if the learner first holds the concrete windowsill plant and a personal guess to revise, and this is the only place the anchor can be introduced.\",\\n              \"id\": \"orient-b1\",\\n              \"intent\": \"orient\",\\n              \"learner_action\": {\\n                \"action\": \"select-one\",\\n                \"purpose\": \"elicit the learner\\'s initial belief so the explanation and contrast sections have a specific wrong model to work against\",\\n                \"target\": \"where the windowsill plant\\'s food comes from\"\\n              }\\n            }\\n          ],\\n          \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n          \"specific_purpose\": \"Put the windowsill plant in front of the learner and get an initial commitment about where its food comes from, so the explanation has something to work against.\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"blocks\": [\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Define producer for a plant: a producer is a living thing that makes its own food. State plainly that the windowsill plant is a producer, so its food is made by the plant itself and is not something delivered to it from outside. Keep the definition to this single idea and do not yet describe how the plant makes the food or what role sunlight plays.\",\\n              \"evidence\": \"The objective\\'s verb is \\'recognize\\' a category, not explain a mechanism, so the slot needs the category term \\'producer\\' fixed precisely before any contrast with soil or water can mean anything.\",\\n              \"id\": \"explain-b1\",\\n              \"intent\": \"define\",\\n              \"learner_action\": null\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Build the idea on the same windowsill plant: the roots draw soil materials and water into the plant, but what enters through the roots is raw material the plant uses, not the plant\\'s food. The food itself is made by the plant. Hold the learner\\'s attention on the plant as the maker and treat soil and water only as intakes, so the soil-as-food and water-as-food readings are undermined without being named as errors yet. Do not introduce the sunlight-as-food idea and do not treat food and energy as interchangeable.\",\\n              \"evidence\": \"Two approved misconceptions both locate food outside the plant, so this block must relocate food-making inside it by separating \\'what the plant takes in\\' from \\'what the plant makes\\' \\\\u2014 a separation a bare definition cannot make.\",\\n              \"id\": \"explain-b2\",\\n              \"intent\": \"explain\",\\n              \"learner_action\": null\\n            }\\n          ],\\n          \"slot_id\": \"explain\",\\n          \"specific_purpose\": \"Establish that the plant is a producer: it makes its own food, while soil materials and water are things it takes in rather than food.\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"blocks\": [\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Take the windowsill plant and put the soil-as-food reading beside the target: one learner says the plant\\'s food is the soil, pulled up through the roots; the producer idea says the plant makes its own food and only draws materials from the soil. Show why the soil reading cannot stand, since the plant still makes food inside itself and the soil is only one of its intakes. Do not repeat the earlier intake-versus-made distinction in full, and do not slide into the water-as-food reading here.\",\\n              \"evidence\": \"The slot\\'s typical intents all treat both sides as legitimate or as a slip; M1 is a held belief that must be surfaced and shut down, so an atypical intent is required and the slot purpose still matches exactly.\",\\n              \"id\": \"contrast-b1\",\\n              \"intent\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n              \"learner_action\": {\\n                \"action\": \"select-one\",\\n                \"purpose\": \"surface whether the learner still holds the soil-as-food model after hearing the target idea\",\\n                \"target\": \"which reading of the windowsill plant matches the producer idea: food made by the plant, or food taken from the soil\"\\n              }\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Set the water-as-food reading against the target on the same windowsill plant beside the cup of water: one learner says the plant\\'s food is the water we give it, since water is what we pour in; the producer idea says the plant makes its own food and the water is an intake, not the food. Make clear that pouring more water does not feed the plant in the sense of food, and that the plant remains the maker. Do not re-run the soil argument and do not treat sunlight as food or as energy here.\",\\n              \"evidence\": \"M2 is a second named belief that places food outside the plant, and because the anchor already includes the cup of water, this block can test that belief against a case the learner has held since the opening instead of a fresh example.\",\\n              \"id\": \"contrast-b2\",\\n              \"intent\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n              \"learner_action\": null\\n            }\\n          ],\\n          \"slot_id\": \"contrast\",\\n          \"specific_purpose\": \"Set the producer idea against the two near-miss readings of the same plant so learners see where the boundary of the idea lies.\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"blocks\": [\\n            {\\n              \"brief\": \"Pose one check that asks the learner to apply the producer idea to the windowsill plant: given that the plant has soil around its roots and water poured in, decide where the plant\\'s food comes from and confirm that the plant is the thing that makes it. Keep the check to this single recognition of the plant as producer, and do not re-explain soil or water as intakes.\",\\n              \"evidence\": \"The objective is a recognition claim about which category the plant belongs to, so the close must read whether the learner places food-making in the plant rather than in the soil or water \\\\u2014 exactly the correct-versus-incorrect signal check-understanding is for.\",\\n              \"id\": \"check-b1\",\\n              \"intent\": \"check-understanding\",\\n              \"learner_action\": {\\n                \"action\": \"select-one\",\\n                \"purpose\": \"measure whether the producer idea displaced the soil-as-food and water-as-food readings after the lesson\",\\n                \"target\": \"where the windowsill plant\\'s food comes from and whether the plant is a producer\"\\n              }\\n            }\\n          ],\\n          \"slot_id\": \"check\",\\n          \"specific_purpose\": \"Check whether the learner now recognizes the plant as a producer that makes its own food, rather than something fed by soil or water.\"\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"teaching_plan_id\": \"c538c330-e276-4aeb-8ff8-278464043dd9\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \"mode\": \"generate\",\\n  \"resolved_policy\": {\\n    \"allow_heuristic_composition_fallback\": true\\n  },\\n  \"scoped_request\": {\\n    \"allow_heuristic_fallback\": true,\\n    \"allowed_kinds\": [\\n      \"callout\",\\n      \"figure\",\\n      \"heading\",\\n      \"list\",\\n      \"paragraph\",\\n      \"table\"\\n    ],\\n    \"path\": \"learn\",\\n    \"stage\": \"document_composition\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nReturn JSON only for this capability payload.'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"properties\": {\"response\": {\"additionalProperties\": true, \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"required\": [\"response\"], \"type\": \"object\", \"title\": \"dict\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Return JSON only for the selected capability payload.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': '{\\n  \"nodes\": [\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"orient-b1-orient-paragraph\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b1\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"kind\": \"paragraph\",\\n      \"role\": \"orient\",\\n      \"reason\": \"Present the concrete windowsill plant beside the cup of water as the anchor case so learners have a specific situation to reason about before any explanation.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"orient-b1-orient-prompt\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"orient-b1\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"kind\": \"callout\",\\n      \"role\": \"elicit-initial-belief\",\\n      \"reason\": \"Signal the commitment prompt clearly, since the learner\\'s initial guess must be on the table before the explanation is introduced; the interaction itself is authored separately.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"explain-b1-heading-producer\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"explain-b1\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"kind\": \"heading\",\\n      \"role\": \"define\",\\n      \"reason\": \"Fix the category term \\'producer\\' as the section\\'s single idea so the definition that follows is easy to locate and reference.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"explain-b1-paragraph-producer-definition\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"explain-b1\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"kind\": \"paragraph\",\\n      \"role\": \"define\",\\n      \"reason\": \"State the definition \u2014 a producer is a living thing that makes its own food \u2014 and apply it plainly to the windowsill plant, without drifting into mechanism or sunlight.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"explain-b2-paragraph-intake-versus-made\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"explain-b2\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"kind\": \"paragraph\",\\n      \"role\": \"explain\",\\n      \"reason\": \"Build the separation on the same plant: roots draw in soil materials and water as raw material, while the food itself is made by the plant, keeping the plant as the maker.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"explain-b2-list-intake-made\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"explain-b2\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"explain\",\\n      \"kind\": \"list\",\\n      \"role\": \"explain\",\\n      \"reason\": \"A short two-part list makes the intake-versus-made distinction visually crisp so learners can hold the boundary rather than blending the two categories.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"contrast-b1-paragraph-soil-reading\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b1\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"kind\": \"paragraph\",\\n      \"role\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n      \"reason\": \"Surface the soil-as-food reading beside the producer idea on the same windowsill plant, so the boundary is visible before the learner is asked to choose.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"contrast-b1-callout-soil-prompt\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b1\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"kind\": \"callout\",\\n      \"role\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n      \"reason\": \"Mark the selection point that asks whether the learner still holds the soil-as-food model; the interaction is authored separately, so only the structural cue belongs here.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"contrast-b1-paragraph-soil-why-fails\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b1\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"kind\": \"paragraph\",\\n      \"role\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n      \"reason\": \"Explain why the soil reading cannot stand \u2014 the plant still makes food inside itself and the soil is only one intake \u2014 without restating the earlier full distinction.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"contrast-b2-heading-water-reading\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b2\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"kind\": \"heading\",\\n      \"role\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n      \"reason\": \"Signal the second near-miss reading explicitly so the water-as-food case is treated as its own contrast, not folded into the soil argument.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"contrast-b2-paragraph-water-reading\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b2\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"kind\": \"paragraph\",\\n      \"role\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n      \"reason\": \"Set the water-as-food reading against the producer idea on the same plant beside the cup of water: pouring more water does not feed the plant in the food sense, and the plant remains the maker.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"contrast-b2-callout-boundary\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"contrast-b2\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"contrast\",\\n      \"kind\": \"callout\",\\n      \"role\": \"highlight-boundary\",\\n      \"reason\": \"A brief boundary reminder \u2014 food is made by the plant, intakes are not food \u2014 locks the key contrast before the closing check without re-running either argument.\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"id\": \"check-b1-paragraph-close\",\\n      \"teaching_block_id\": \"check-b1\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"check\",\\n      \"kind\": \"paragraph\",\\n      \"role\": \"check-understanding\",\\n      \"reason\": \"Pose the single closing recognition task on the windowsill plant so the learner applies the producer idea rather than reviewing soil or water as separate cases.\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '1 validation error:\\n```json\\n[\\n  {\\n    \"type\": \"missing\",\\n    \"loc\": [\\n      \"response\"\\n    ],\\n    \"msg\": \"Field required\"\\n  }\\n]\\n```\\n\\nFix the errors and try again.'}], 'model': 'deepseek-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 8000, 'stream': False}, 'extra_json': {'thinking': {'type': 'disabled'}}}"}
