{"timestamp": "2026-09-13T20:59:34.609299+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-c2b6f9df-db65-4c56-a338-b3b0aaed42ce', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You author one already-selected educational capability. Follow the\\nsupplied AuthoringDefinition and exact output schema. Preserve block identity, objective, scope,\\nlearner action, source ownership and assessment mode. Do not select another capability or redesign\\nthe teaching plan.\\n\\nPlanning instructions are not final content. For an activity, produce a meaningful prompt, task\\ndata, justified answer relationships and useful feedback as required by the contract. Do not infer\\ncorrectness from option positions, number/word positions, example ordering or arbitrary defaults.\\nDo not copy illustrative examples as unrelated lesson content.\\n\\nTreat approved items as authoritative content. Conversion must preserve their question and answer\\nmeaning. Report incompatibility through the defined error path instead of guessing. Use supported\\nteacher-review only when the work order policy permits it.\\n\\nReturn exactly the selected output schema. Do not emit sibling schemas, markdown wrappers, internal\\nplanning metadata or extra fields. If required information is absent, use the configured\\nmissing-input mechanism; do not create placeholder content to satisfy structure.\\n\\nDo not invent or overwrite knowledge/assessment policy fields. Effective policy is code-owned.\\n\\n## KNOWLEDGE POLICY\\nKnowledge policy: supplied_preferred. Use supplied facts as the primary basis; you may add relevant model knowledge within the objective and constraints. Do not describe model knowledge as approved factual material.\\n\\n## PACKAGE CAPABILITY INSTRUCTIONS\\nCapability: choice.\\r\\n\\r\\nAuthor a complete activity envelope: student-facing prompt, choice config, and feedback.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Write the prompt as a clear question the learner reads directly. The planning brief is context only \u2014 do not copy it verbatim.\\r\\n- Provide feedback.correct and feedback.incorrect messages tied to the question and distractors.\\r\\n- Put options and the correct option id in config.\\r\\n\\r\\n- Use at least two options with unique stable ids.\\r\\n- Exactly one option is correct.\\r\\n- Distractors must be plausible and tied to a stateable misconception.\\r\\n- Do not use this for questions with several defensible answers.\\n\\n## AUTHORING DEFINITION\\n{\\n  \"assessment\": {\\n    \"default\": \"automatic_required\",\\n    \"supported\": [\\n      \"automatic_required\"\\n    ],\\n    \"teacher_review_permitted\": false\\n  },\\n  \"capability_id\": \"choice\",\\n  \"converter_ref\": \"learn.choice.approved_item_converter\",\\n  \"definition_hash\": \"9c9eca46dacb6c6603192a541ee7c019236a8ab713137ae9027d3e3557c1c7eb\",\\n  \"instructions\": \"Capability: choice.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAuthor a complete activity envelope: student-facing prompt, choice config, and feedback.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Write the prompt as a clear question the learner reads directly. The planning brief is context only \\\\u2014 do not copy it verbatim.\\\\r\\\\n- Provide feedback.correct and feedback.incorrect messages tied to the question and distractors.\\\\r\\\\n- Put options and the correct option id in config.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Use at least two options with unique stable ids.\\\\r\\\\n- Exactly one option is correct.\\\\r\\\\n- Distractors must be plausible and tied to a stateable misconception.\\\\r\\\\n- Do not use this for questions with several defensible answers.\",\\n  \"knowledge\": {\\n    \"default\": \"supplied_preferred\",\\n    \"supported\": [\\n      \"supplied_only\",\\n      \"supplied_preferred\",\\n      \"objective_development\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \"modes\": [\\n    \"generate\",\\n    \"convert-approved\"\\n  ],\\n  \"native_path\": \"learn\",\\n  \"payload_schema\": {\\n    \"additionalProperties\": true,\\n    \"properties\": {\\n      \"config\": {\\n        \"$id\": \"learn/choice/config.v1\",\\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n        \"properties\": {\\n          \"correct_option_id\": {\\n            \"minLength\": 1,\\n            \"type\": \"string\"\\n          },\\n          \"options\": {\\n            \"items\": {\\n              \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n              \"properties\": {\\n                \"explanation\": {\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                },\\n                \"id\": {\\n                  \"minLength\": 1,\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                },\\n                \"text\": {\\n                  \"minLength\": 1,\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                }\\n              },\\n              \"required\": [\\n                \"id\",\\n                \"text\"\\n              ],\\n              \"type\": \"object\"\\n            },\\n            \"minItems\": 2,\\n            \"type\": \"array\",\\n            \"uniqueItems\": true\\n          },\\n          \"presentation\": {\\n            \"enum\": [\\n              \"text\",\\n              \"image\"\\n            ]\\n          }\\n        },\\n        \"required\": [\\n          \"options\",\\n          \"correct_option_id\"\\n        ],\\n        \"type\": \"object\"\\n      },\\n      \"feedback\": {\\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n        \"properties\": {\\n          \"correct\": {\\n            \"type\": \"string\"\\n          },\\n          \"incorrect\": {\\n            \"type\": \"string\"\\n          },\\n          \"partial\": {\\n            \"type\": \"string\"\\n          }\\n        },\\n        \"required\": [\\n          \"correct\",\\n          \"incorrect\"\\n        ],\\n        \"type\": \"object\"\\n      },\\n      \"prompt\": {\\n        \"minLength\": 1,\\n        \"type\": \"string\"\\n      }\\n    },\\n    \"required\": [\\n      \"prompt\",\\n      \"config\",\\n      \"feedback\"\\n    ],\\n    \"type\": \"object\"\\n  },\\n  \"required_inputs\": [\\n    \"teaching_plan_block\",\\n    \"learn_selection_decision\",\\n    \"lesson_context\",\\n    \"allowed_facts\",\\n    \"terminology\",\\n    \"learner_action\",\\n    \"approved_items_when_converting\"\\n  ],\\n  \"validator_refs\": [\\n    \"learn.payload_schema\",\\n    \"learn.evaluateChoice\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\n## SCOPED REQUEST\\n{\\n  \"inputs\": {\\n    \"allowed_facts\": [\\n      \"plants have roots, stems and leaves\",\\n      \"living things need food to grow\",\\n      \"Plants are living things that can produce their own food\",\\n      \"Plants are called producers\",\\n      \"Use one concrete classroom example.\",\\n      \"Explain that plants make their own food (are producers)\",\\n      \"Identify leaves as the site of photosynthesis and chlorophyll as the light-capturing substance\",\\n      \"Describe photosynthesis as using light, carbon dioxide, and water to produce food and oxygen\",\\n      \"Explain why light is essential for photosynthesis\"\\n    ],\\n    \"approved_items_when_converting\": [],\\n    \"learn_selection_decision\": {\\n      \"capability_id\": \"choice\",\\n      \"lane\": \"interaction\",\\n      \"support_level\": null\\n    },\\n    \"learner_action\": \"select-one\",\\n    \"lesson_context\": {\\n      \"input_availability\": \"supplied_statements\",\\n      \"objective\": \"Recognize that plants are producers that make their own food\",\\n      \"subject\": \"Science\",\\n      \"teaching_plan_revision\": 1,\\n      \"title\": \"The lesson opens on the classroom plant on the windowsill beside the cup of water and asks learners to commit to a guess about where its food comes from, so a personal wrong model is on the table. The explanation then fixes the category term \\\\u2014 the plant is a producer, a living thing that makes its own food \\\\u2014 and separates what the plant takes in through its roots from what it makes. The contrast section puts the producer idea against the soil-as-food and water-as-food readings on the same plant so the boundary is visible, and the close checks whether the learner now recognizes the plant, not the soil or the water, as the maker of the food.\"\\n    },\\n    \"teaching_plan_block\": {\\n      \"action\": \"select-one\",\\n      \"block_id\": \"check-b1\",\\n      \"brief\": \"Pose one check that asks the learner to apply the producer idea to the windowsill plant: given that the plant has soil around its roots and water poured in, decide where the plant\\'s food comes from and confirm that the plant is the thing that makes it. Keep the check to this single recognition of the plant as producer, and do not re-explain soil or water as intakes.\",\\n      \"evidence\": \"The objective is a recognition claim about which category the plant belongs to, so the close must read whether the learner places food-making in the plant rather than in the soil or water \\\\u2014 exactly the correct-versus-incorrect signal check-understanding is for.\",\\n      \"intent\": \"check-understanding\",\\n      \"section_id\": \"check\"\\n    },\\n    \"terminology\": []\\n  },\\n  \"mode\": \"generate\",\\n  \"resolved_policy\": {\\n    \"assessment_policy_source\": \"package:1.0.0\",\\n    \"definition_hash\": \"9c9eca46dacb6c6603192a541ee7c019236a8ab713137ae9027d3e3557c1c7eb\",\\n    \"definition_version\": \"2.0.0\",\\n    \"effective_assessment_policy\": \"automatic_required\",\\n    \"effective_knowledge_policy\": \"supplied_preferred\",\\n    \"executed_evaluation_mode\": \"accepted-answers\",\\n    \"executed_knowledge_mode\": \"supplied_facts\",\\n    \"fallback_reason\": null,\\n    \"input_availability\": \"supplied_statements\",\\n    \"input_revision\": null,\\n    \"knowledge_policy_source\": \"package:1.0.0\",\\n    \"policy_version\": \"1.0.0\",\\n    \"requested_assessment_policy\": null,\\n    \"requested_knowledge_policy\": null,\\n    \"teacher_review_permitted\": false\\n  },\\n  \"scoped_request\": {\\n    \"action\": \"select-one\",\\n    \"allowed_facts\": [\\n      \"plants have roots, stems and leaves\",\\n      \"living things need food to grow\",\\n      \"Plants are living things that can produce their own food\",\\n      \"Plants are called producers\",\\n      \"Use one concrete classroom example.\",\\n      \"Explain that plants make their own food (are producers)\",\\n      \"Identify leaves as the site of photosynthesis and chlorophyll as the light-capturing substance\",\\n      \"Describe photosynthesis as using light, carbon dioxide, and water to produce food and oxygen\",\\n      \"Explain why light is essential for photosynthesis\"\\n    ],\\n    \"authoring_definition\": {\\n      \"assessment\": {\\n        \"default\": \"automatic_required\",\\n        \"supported\": [\\n          \"automatic_required\"\\n        ],\\n        \"teacher_review_permitted\": false\\n      },\\n      \"asset_requirements\": null,\\n      \"capability_id\": \"choice\",\\n      \"capacity\": {\\n        \"optionMaxWords\": 20,\\n        \"optionsMax\": 5,\\n        \"optionsMin\": 2,\\n        \"stemMaxWords\": 40\\n      },\\n      \"config_schema\": {\\n        \"$id\": \"learn/choice/config.v1\",\\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n        \"properties\": {\\n          \"correct_option_id\": {\\n            \"minLength\": 1,\\n            \"type\": \"string\"\\n          },\\n          \"options\": {\\n            \"items\": {\\n              \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n              \"properties\": {\\n                \"explanation\": {\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                },\\n                \"id\": {\\n                  \"minLength\": 1,\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                },\\n                \"text\": {\\n                  \"minLength\": 1,\\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\\n                }\\n              },\\n              \"required\": [\\n                \"id\",\\n                \"text\"\\n              ],\\n              \"type\": \"object\"\\n            },\\n            \"minItems\": 2,\\n            \"type\": \"array\",\\n            \"uniqueItems\": true\\n          },\\n          \"presentation\": {\\n            \"enum\": [\\n              \"text\",\\n              \"image\"\\n            ]\\n          }\\n        },\\n        \"required\": [\\n          \"options\",\\n          \"correct_option_id\"\\n        ],\\n        \"type\": \"object\"\\n      },\\n      \"converter_ref\": \"learn.choice.approved_item_converter\",\\n      \"definition_hash\": \"9c9eca46dacb6c6603192a541ee7c019236a8ab713137ae9027d3e3557c1c7eb\",\\n      \"definition_version\": \"2.0.0\",\\n      \"examples\": [\\n        {\\n          \"correct_option_id\": \"air\",\\n          \"options\": [\\n            {\\n              \"explanation\": \"Mass is not drawn from soil.\",\\n              \"id\": \"soil\",\\n              \"text\": \"From the soil\"\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \"id\": \"air\",\\n              \"text\": \"From carbon dioxide in the air\"\\n            },\\n            {\\n              \"explanation\": \"Light supplies energy, not mass.\",\\n              \"id\": \"light\",\\n              \"text\": \"From sunlight alone\"\\n            }\\n          ]\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"field_guidance\": {\\n        \"config.correct_option_id\": \"Must equal the id of exactly one declared option.\",\\n        \"config.options\": \"Stable ids, parallel grammatical form. Give each wrong option an explanation naming the misconception it reveals.\",\\n        \"config.presentation\": \"\\'image\\' renders options as pictures; evaluation is identical, so do not author a separate kind for it.\",\\n        \"feedback.correct\": \"Short message shown when the learner answer is fully correct.\",\\n        \"feedback.incorrect\": \"Short message shown when the learner answer is wrong or incomplete.\",\\n        \"feedback.partial\": \"Optional message when partial credit applies; omit when the interaction does not support partial scoring.\",\\n        \"prompt\": \"Student-facing question or instruction. Use plain language the learner reads directly; do not copy the planning brief.\"\\n      },\\n      \"id\": \"choice\",\\n      \"instructions\": {\\n        \"resource_ref\": \"contracts/authoring/instructions/choice-writer-v1.txt\",\\n        \"text\": \"Capability: choice.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAuthor a complete activity envelope: student-facing prompt, choice config, and feedback.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Write the prompt as a clear question the learner reads directly. The planning brief is context only \\\\u2014 do not copy it verbatim.\\\\r\\\\n- Provide feedback.correct and feedback.incorrect messages tied to the question and distractors.\\\\r\\\\n- Put options and the correct option id in config.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Use at least two options with unique stable ids.\\\\r\\\\n- Exactly one option is correct.\\\\r\\\\n- Distractors must be plausible and tied to a stateable misconception.\\\\r\\\\n- Do not use this for questions with several defensible answers.\"\\n      },\\n      \"knowledge\": {\\n        \"default\": \"supplied_preferred\",\\n        \"supported\": [\\n          \"supplied_only\",\\n          \"supplied_preferred\",\\n          \"objective_development\"\\n        ]\\n      },\\n      \"lane\": \"interaction\",\\n      \"modes\": [\\n        \"generate\",\\n        \"convert-approved\"\\n      ],\\n      \"native_path\": \"learn\",\\n      \"negative_cases\": [\\n        \"a single option\",\\n        \"duplicate option ids\",\\n        \"correct_option_id naming an option that is not declared\",\\n        \"a distractor no learner would choose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"payload_schema\": {\\n        \"additionalProperties\": true,\\n        \"properties\": {\\n          \"config\": {\\n            \"$id\": \"learn/choice/config.v1\",\\n            \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n            \"properties\": {\\n              \"correct_option_id\": {\\n                \"minLength\": 1,\\n                \"type\": \"string\"\\n              },\\n              \"options\": {\\n                \"items\": {\\n                  \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n                  \"properties\": {\\n                    \"explanation\": {\\n                      \"type\": \"string\"\\n                    },\\n                    \"id\": {\\n                      \"minLength\": 1,\\n                      \"type\": \"string\"\\n                    },\\n                    \"text\": {\\n                      \"minLength\": 1,\\n                      \"type\": \"string\"\\n                    }\\n                  },\\n                  \"required\": [\\n                    \"id\",\\n                    \"text\"\\n                  ],\\n                  \"type\": \"object\"\\n                },\\n                \"minItems\": 2,\\n                \"type\": \"array\",\\n                \"uniqueItems\": true\\n              },\\n              \"presentation\": {\\n                \"enum\": [\\n                  \"text\",\\n                  \"image\"\\n                ]\\n              }\\n            },\\n            \"required\": [\\n              \"options\",\\n              \"correct_option_id\"\\n            ],\\n            \"type\": \"object\"\\n          },\\n          \"feedback\": {\\n            \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n            \"properties\": {\\n              \"correct\": {\\n                \"type\": \"string\"\\n              },\\n              \"incorrect\": {\\n                \"type\": \"string\"\\n              },\\n              \"partial\": {\\n                \"type\": \"string\"\\n              }\\n            },\\n            \"required\": [\\n              \"correct\",\\n              \"incorrect\"\\n            ],\\n            \"type\": \"object\"\\n          },\\n          \"prompt\": {\\n            \"minLength\": 1,\\n            \"type\": \"string\"\\n          }\\n        },\\n        \"required\": [\\n          \"prompt\",\\n          \"config\",\\n          \"feedback\"\\n        ],\\n        \"type\": \"object\"\\n      },\\n      \"payload_schema_ref\": \"learn/choice/config.v1\",\\n      \"purpose\": \"Let a learner choose the one correct option from a closed set.\",\\n      \"required_inputs\": [\\n        \"teaching_plan_block\",\\n        \"learn_selection_decision\",\\n        \"lesson_context\",\\n        \"allowed_facts\",\\n        \"terminology\",\\n        \"learner_action\",\\n        \"approved_items_when_converting\"\\n      ],\\n      \"requires\": [\\n        \"at least two options with unique non-empty ids\",\\n        \"exactly one correct_option_id, and it must name a declared option\",\\n        \"keyboard-operable option selection\"\\n      ],\\n      \"schema_ref\": \"learn/choice/config.v1\",\\n      \"source_refs\": [\\n        \"apps/textbook-agent/frontend/src/lib/learn/interactions/ChoiceInteraction.svelte\",\\n        \"contracts/authoring/instructions/choice-writer-v1.txt\",\\n        \"learn/choice/config.v1\",\\n        \"apps/textbook-agent/frontend/src/lib/learn/interactions/interaction-contract.ts#evaluateChoice\"\\n      ],\\n      \"validator_refs\": [\\n        \"learn.payload_schema\",\\n        \"learn.evaluateChoice\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"authoring_mode\": \"new\",\\n    \"block_id\": \"check-b1\",\\n    \"brief\": \"Pose one check that asks the learner to apply the producer idea to the windowsill plant: given that the plant has soil around its roots and water poured in, decide where the plant\\'s food comes from and confirm that the plant is the thing that makes it. Keep the check to this single recognition of the plant as producer, and do not re-explain soil or water as intakes.\",\\n    \"capability_contract_hash\": \"9c9eca46dacb6c6603192a541ee7c019236a8ab713137ae9027d3e3557c1c7eb\",\\n    \"capability_id\": \"choice\",\\n    \"definition_hash\": \"9c9eca46dacb6c6603192a541ee7c019236a8ab713137ae9027d3e3557c1c7eb\",\\n    \"dependency_ids\": [],\\n    \"evidence\": \"The objective is a recognition claim about which category the plant belongs to, so the close must read whether the learner places food-making in the plant rather than in the soil or water \\\\u2014 exactly the correct-versus-incorrect signal check-understanding is for.\",\\n    \"executed_knowledge_mode\": \"supplied_facts\",\\n    \"field_guidance\": {\\n      \"config.correct_option_id\": \"Must equal the id of exactly one declared option.\",\\n      \"config.options\": \"Stable ids, parallel grammatical form. Give each wrong option an explanation naming the misconception it reveals.\",\\n      \"config.presentation\": \"\\'image\\' renders options as pictures; evaluation is identical, so do not author a separate kind for it.\",\\n      \"feedback.correct\": \"Short message shown when the learner answer is fully correct.\",\\n      \"feedback.incorrect\": \"Short message shown when the learner answer is wrong or incomplete.\",\\n      \"feedback.partial\": \"Optional message when partial credit applies; omit when the interaction does not support partial scoring.\",\\n      \"prompt\": \"Student-facing question or instruction. Use plain language the learner reads directly; do not copy the planning brief.\"\\n    },\\n    \"input_availability\": \"supplied_statements\",\\n    \"instructions\": \"# Interaction Writer Policy\\\\n\\\\nWrite one learner interaction for the already selected interaction kind.\\\\n\\\\nThe interaction must:\\\\n- directly implement the Teaching Plan learner action;\\\\n- use supplied lesson context/facts/terminology;\\\\n- avoid introducing untaught knowledge;\\\\n- have a clear prompt;\\\\n- have plausible distractors/items where relevant;\\\\n- contain a valid answer/evaluation contract;\\\\n- avoid placeholder language;\\\\n- avoid copying the Teaching Plan brief verbatim;\\\\n- match requested difficulty;\\\\n- be answerable from lesson state available at this point.\\\\n\\\\nDo not change the interaction kind. Do not add another learner task. Do not write content that belongs in neighboring document nodes.\\\\n\\\\nWhen converting an approved assessment item, preserve approved meaning and answer ownership.\\\\n\\\\n\\\\nCapability: choice.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\nAuthor a complete activity envelope: student-facing prompt, choice config, and feedback.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Write the prompt as a clear question the learner reads directly. The planning brief is context only \\\\u2014 do not copy it verbatim.\\\\r\\\\n- Provide feedback.correct and feedback.incorrect messages tied to the question and distractors.\\\\r\\\\n- Put options and the correct option id in config.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n- Use at least two options with unique stable ids.\\\\r\\\\n- Exactly one option is correct.\\\\r\\\\n- Distractors must be plausible and tied to a stateable misconception.\\\\r\\\\n- Do not use this for questions with several defensible answers.\",\\n    \"intent\": \"check-understanding\",\\n    \"lane\": \"interaction\",\\n    \"modes\": [\\n      \"generate\",\\n      \"convert-approved\"\\n    ],\\n    \"payload_schema\": {\\n      \"additionalProperties\": true,\\n      \"properties\": {\\n        \"config\": {\\n          \"$id\": \"learn/choice/config.v1\",\\n          \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n          \"properties\": {\\n            \"correct_option_id\": {\\n              \"minLength\": 1,\\n              \"type\": \"string\"\\n            },\\n            \"options\": {\\n              \"items\": {\\n                \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n                \"properties\": {\\n                  \"explanation\": {\\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\\n                  },\\n                  \"id\": {\\n                    \"minLength\": 1,\\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\\n                  },\\n                  \"text\": {\\n                    \"minLength\": 1,\\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\\n                  }\\n                },\\n                \"required\": [\\n                  \"id\",\\n                  \"text\"\\n                ],\\n                \"type\": \"object\"\\n              },\\n              \"minItems\": 2,\\n              \"type\": \"array\",\\n              \"uniqueItems\": true\\n            },\\n            \"presentation\": {\\n              \"enum\": [\\n                \"text\",\\n                \"image\"\\n              ]\\n            }\\n          },\\n          \"required\": [\\n            \"options\",\\n            \"correct_option_id\"\\n          ],\\n          \"type\": \"object\"\\n        },\\n        \"feedback\": {\\n          \"additionalProperties\": false,\\n          \"properties\": {\\n            \"correct\": {\\n              \"type\": \"string\"\\n            },\\n            \"incorrect\": {\\n              \"type\": \"string\"\\n            },\\n            \"partial\": {\\n              \"type\": \"string\"\\n            }\\n          },\\n          \"required\": [\\n            \"correct\",\\n            \"incorrect\"\\n          ],\\n          \"type\": \"object\"\\n        },\\n        \"prompt\": {\\n          \"minLength\": 1,\\n          \"type\": \"string\"\\n        }\\n      },\\n      \"required\": [\\n        \"prompt\",\\n        \"config\",\\n        \"feedback\"\\n      ],\\n      \"type\": \"object\"\\n    },\\n    \"required_inputs\": [\\n      \"teaching_plan_block\",\\n      \"learn_selection_decision\",\\n      \"lesson_context\",\\n      \"allowed_facts\",\\n      \"terminology\",\\n      \"learner_action\",\\n      \"approved_items_when_converting\"\\n    